        {
          "id": 474678770,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I'm a bit puzzled here. In the line I changed, there is a test on `item`'s existence. How would a call to this function be correct with item == NULL? Moreover `item` has been already used here, then I don't really see the point of this check. For what I can see we (alternatively) should:\n\n1. check params validity (we don't trust the caller): `item` should be checked as soon as possible, as well as `fields`\n1. trust the caller: neither `item` or `fields` should be checked, but in this case a buggy caller leads to a crash.\n\nAny thoughts?",
          "author": {
            "id": 277876,
            "username": "crondaemon",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-28T15:00:13.138Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-28T15:00:13.138Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 82991197,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
