            "name": "Dario Lombardo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/143ae7a6f9e11c9eed24a7fdb44bb40d442fd274ba01a2e3a4abe1596819bea2?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/crondaemon"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2020-12-29T16:40:27.167Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1472,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 474725730,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Hi,\nIt seems to me like `proto_item_add_bitmask_tree()` is called internally in proto.c with item = NULL. But I don't see how calling it without \"fields\" could serve any purpose. I did not find any example in packet-couchbase.c, line number?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
